{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATIONAL STATUS + INTERIM MITIGATION APPLIED (2026-08-13 session cd66bacc).\n\nState check of the shared tracker: working tree CLEAN, ahead/behind origin = 0/0 (a prior session's recovery held or the deletions were committed). Latent exposure remains: 119 */.archived and 126 */.write.lock files are still TRACKED in HEAD (committed before the gitignore patterns), so any interrupted sweep re-creates abort variant (b).\n\nINTERIM MITIGATION now active machine-wide: compact.trigger = \"off\" set in the XDG user config (~/.config/rebar/config.toml). The project rebar.toml does not set compact.trigger, so user-level off governs every worktree/session on this machine (precedence: project > user, and project is silent). This removes the dirty-tree seed until the crash-atomicity fix here lands. REMOVE the user-config block when closing this ticket.\n\nFix program being structured as an epic covering: crash-atomic fold (this ticket), reconverge variant (b) recovery, push-recovery parity (sulfuryl-suicidal-osprey), untracking */.archived + */.write.lock from HEAD via a sanctioned migration, fsck/doctor self-heal tooling for this class, and active-only scan scoping with an override flag."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786677036631872001,"uuid":"aec55542-73fb-42bf-975e-299f773a3635"}